# Techno Products – AI-Powered Sales & Service Chatbot

## 1. Project Overview

Techno Products Sales & Service Bot is an AI-powered multilingual chatbot developed using Python, Streamlit, LangChain, Hugging Face, Qdrant and Groq.

The main objective of this project is to help customers quickly find industrial product information and receive basic service-related assistance through natural language questions in Tamil or English.

Instead of manually searching through a large product catalogue, customers can ask questions such as:

- What is the price of an M30 bolt?
- What is the stock availability of a 2HP motor?
- மோட்டார் சத்தம் வருவதற்கு என்ன காரணம்?

The chatbot retrieves relevant information from the industrial product catalogue and uses an LLM to generate a contextual response.

## 2. Project Objectives

- Build a multilingual AI chatbot for industrial products.
- Retrieve relevant information from product catalogues.
- Provide product prices and stock information.
- Answer basic customer service-related questions.
- Reduce manual searching and improve customer support.

## 3. Technologies Used

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Python | Core programming language |
| Streamlit | Chatbot user interface |
| LangChain | Document processing and retrieval integration |
| Hugging Face | Multilingual embedding model |
| MiniLM | Converts text into vector embeddings |
| Qdrant | Vector database for storing and searching embeddings |
| Groq | LLM inference and answer generation |
| Python-dotenv | Loads environment variables securely |

## 4. Project Architecture

The project follows a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) architecture.

### Data Ingestion – ingest.py

1. Loads the industrial product catalogue.
2. Splits the document into smaller chunks using RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter.
3. Converts the text chunks into vector embeddings using Hugging Face.
4. Stores the embeddings in the Qdrant vector database.

### Question Answering – app.py

1. Accepts customer questions through Streamlit.
2. Converts the question into an embedding using the same embedding model.
3. Searches Qdrant for the five most relevant document chunks.
4. Passes the retrieved context and customer question to the Groq LLM.
5. Generates a contextual answer.
6. Displays the answer and retrieved source documents.

